== Solution 5 (Summation Notation) ==
We solve thiss using the <imath>\textbf{Sigma Function}</imath> (summation notation).

The sequence starts at:
\[
a_1 = 1
\]

Each term increases by a growing difference:
\[
\begin{aligned}
a_2 &= a_1 + 6 = 7 \\
a_3 &= a_2 + 12 = 19 \\
a_4 &= a_3 + 18 = 37
\end{aligned}
\]

We observe that the difference added at each step forms an arithmetic sequence:  
\[
6,\, 12,\, 18,\, 24,\, \dots = 6k \text{ for } k = 1, 2, 3, \dots
\]

To express this with the \textbf{Sigma Function}, we write the <imath>n</imath>-th term as:

a_n = 1 + \sum_{k=1}^{n-1} 6k
\]

This is a standard arithmetic sum, so we use the formula:
\[
\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} k = \frac{(n-1)n}{2}
\]

Substitute this in:
\[
a_n = 1 + 6 \cdot \frac{(n-1)n}{2}
\]

When we simplify:
\[
a_n = 1 + 3n(n - 1)
\]
\[
\boxed{a_n = 1 + 3n(n - 1)}
\]

Let’s compute the 4th term using the sigma-based formula:
\[
a_4 = 1 + 3 \cdot 4 \cdot (4 - 1) = 1 + 3 \cdot 12 = 1 + 36 = \boxed{37}
\]
So the answer is 37.

==Solution 6 (Quick)==

Notice that the middle row, which is also the row with the most dots in it, has the same number of dots as the topmost or bottommost row multiplied by 2, then minus one. Since the new hexagon will have four dots at the topmost and bottommost rows, the middle row will have (4*2)-1=7 dots. Also, notice that the rows increase in the number of dots from the topmost to the middle row, then decrease from the middle row to the bottommost row by 1. So, noticing these patterns, the amount of dots in the next hexagon is simply <imath>4+5+6+7+6+5+4=\boxed{\textbf{(B) }37}</imath> dots.~Evžen D.

==Solution 7 (Fast Patern Recognition)==

The first hexagon has <imath>1</imath> dot in it. The second hexagon has <imath>7</imath> dots in it. The third hexagon has <imath>19</imath> dots on it. From the first to the second, we add <imath>6</imath> hexagons. From the second to the third, we add <imath>12</imath> hexagons. Therefore, recognizing the pattern, from the third to the fourth case, we have to add <imath>18</imath> dots to the <imath>19</imath> we already have, resulting in our answer of <imath>\boxed{\textbf{(B) }37}</imath> dots.

~BryBro7

